PB  - Springer Nature Switzerland
CY  - Cham
AB  - Research on large language models (LLMs) is a prominent field in open-world machine learning. Despite their significant capabilities in natural language processing, LLMs face several challenges that must be overcome, namely, consistency, hallucinations and jailbreaking. In this work we focus on the latter. Jailbreak attacks involve crafting prompts designed to bypass the model alignment safeguards of LLMs, leading to harmful outputs that compromise the safety of the LLM model.
